      "writtenOn": "2023-06-29T18:38:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe it\u0027s a non-issue, but I\u0027m surprised to see floats being used in EC code.\n\nPresumably we can\u0027t guarantee the presence of an FPU, so we are pulling in the software libraries to handle this. Is this increasing the size of the EC binary, or are those libraries already present in the build?\n\nLooking around a bit, there is `src/platform/ec/core/cortex-m/include/fpu.h`, though that won\u0027t apply to other chipsets like RISC-V. It also looks most other EC code uses fixed point, via `FLOAT_TO_FP()`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
