      "writtenOn": "2023-07-04T11:45:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Zephyr supports FPU for Cortex-M0/M3 and RISC-V RV32i. AFAIK most modern ECs do have hardware FP unit.\n\nUnfortunately, if we want to use fixed-point for filter calculations it should rather be a uint64 where mul/div is not efficient on 32-bit architectures.\nI assumed that Google targets in ECs in such price range that we can rely that FPU is there.",
