      "writtenOn": "2023-06-29T18:38:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How does the legacy algorithm work with these redefined KConfig values? Meaning, how can the same Kconfig values be used in different algorithms, being interpreted in different ways?\n\nSpecifically, `common/body_detection_legacy.c` is now using `4000` as the new default value, but interpreting it with the old `(mm/s^2)^2` units while the new `common/body_detection.c` is interpreting it as `uG`.\n\nThese values either:\n1. Need to be duplicated, with the appropriate values/units for each algorithm. Or,\n2. We drop support for the old algorithm.\n\nOtherwise, reusing the same Kconfig definitions is a bug when used in the old algorithm code.",
      "revId": "f4117c9a1f37c174610e10667a2cbd877d40a900",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
